In our project, every developer created a separate feature branch from develop. Once development was completed, 
a Pull Request was raised. Before merging, code reviews, build validation, SonarQube scans, and testing were performed.
If multiple developers worked on the same code area, they first synced their branch with the latest develop branch and resolved any merge conflicts.
We mainly used Squash Merge through Azure DevOps to keep the Git history clean and easy to maintain.






